<title>AUSTRALIA: Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in last year.</title>
<headline>Biggest gains/falls for ASX 100 index in last year.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a list of the 10 largest gaining and falling stocks for Australian companies included in the Australian Stock Exchange's ASX 100 index for the year to August 1.</p>
<p>Top 10 largest gains in year</p>
<p>Rank Name			 Price     pct change</p>
<p> 1  Oil Search		   4.16	 208.15</p>
<p> 2  Sthn Pac Pete		3.51	 123.57</p>
<p> 3  Macquarie Bank	    13.78	  99.71</p>
<p> 4  Fletcher-Energy div	4.64	  70.12</p>
<p> 5  A N Z Bank		  10.70	  67.45</p>
<p> 6  Seven Network		5.85	  64.79</p>
<p> 7  Natl Aust Bank	    19.51	  64.64</p>
<p> 8  Howard Smith		13.15	  62.55</p>
<p> 9  Goodman Fielder	    2.10	  61.54</p>
<p>10  Wesfarmers		  12.28	  59.90</p>
<p>Top 10 largest falls in year</p>
<p>Rank Name			 Price     pct change</p>
<p> 1  Davids Limited	     0.89	 -47.65</p>
<p> 2  Newcrest Mining	    2.72	 -44.15</p>
<p> 3  Sons Of Gwalia	     5.00	 -39.02</p>
<p> 4  Goldfields		   1.74	 -38.73</p>
<p> 5  RGC			    4.16	 -32.36</p>
<p> 6  Plutonic Rsc		 4.00	 -31.03</p>
<p> 7  Great Central		2.78	 -23.84</p>
<p> 8  Crown			  2.17	 -21.71</p>
<p> 9  Normandy Min		 1.57	 -21.50</p>
<p>10  Village Roadshow	   4.75	 -16.96</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
